# Lab 2 – Service Version Detection

## Command

```bash
nmap -sV 127.0.0.1
```

### Purpose

Detect the version of services running on open ports.

### What I Learned

The `-sV` option helps identify the software and version behind an open port, which is useful during vulnerability assessments.

---

# Lab 3 – Scan All TCP Ports

## Command

```bash
nmap -p- 127.0.0.1
```

### Purpose

Scan all 65,535 TCP ports instead of only the default 1,000.

### What I Learned

A service may run on an uncommon port. Scanning every port helps discover services that a default scan could miss.

---

# Lab 4 – Operating System Detection

## Command

```bash
sudo nmap -O 127.0.0.1
```

### Purpose

Attempt to identify the operating system of the target.

### Note

OS detection is generally more accurate when scanning another host rather than the local machine.

